    "created_at": "2026-03-16T10:24:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-16T10:25:35Z",
    "body": "> What does \"marking as obsolete\" mean? Perhaps that will help with the discussion?\n\nIt's a form of deprecation, I think the MDN warning is sometimes a bit heavy handed, it's not to say hey browsers are going to unship this, it's just saying this feature exists for historical reasons but there's an alternative and we recommend you use it instead. It's a clearer signal imo that future features won't necessarily get added to these input buttons (e.g. interestfor also won't be supported on input buttons). Also stuff such as linters might start to suggest against usage.\n\nWe do have possible oppurtunites to steer people away from them too (not adding new HTML features is one, but we could also not support appearance base on them (not sure how others would feel about that) if that was something we wanted to do.\n\nThough it is true they're not actively harmful, imo neither was marquee and that is obsoleted, so I think it's still possibly worthwhile though obviously I defer to the editors and conformance people ultimately, just thought I'd raise the discussion.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
