    "created_at": "2026-03-16T13:33:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-16T13:33:40Z",
    "body": "I think it's not a good use of web developers time to replace `<input type=button>` with `<button type=button>`, or for submit/reset. There should be a good reason to make something obsolete that makes it not a waste of time for developers to get an error when using a conformance checker and fixing that error. Not supporting command/commandfor doesn't seem like a strong enough reason. Nor the lack of rich content or slightly more [limited styling](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#button-layout-2) (when that is needed, they can switch the element at that point).\n\nWe don't have an official status of \"not obsolete but we're not adding new features\", even though that happens in practice (e.g. the `object` element vs `iframe`).\n\ncc @sideshowbarker ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
